/**
 * The CrowdBuzz logo.
 *
 * A torn-off ticket stub with the "c" punched out of it, beside the name.
 * Both are OUTLINES, not live text: the glyphs were pulled out of Bricolage
 * Grotesque at weight 800 — the same face and weight the site sets in — and
 * baked to paths. That matters for a logo. It cannot reflow when the webfont
 * is slow, cannot shift if Google ever revises the family, and drops into a
 * favicon or an email with nothing to load.
 *
 * The hole in the stub is a real hole (fill-rule evenodd over one path), so
 * whatever is behind the logo shows through it. That is why there is no
 * hardcoded background colour anywhere in here, and why the mark works on the
 * night, on paper and on coral without a second drawing.
 *
 * Generated geometry — do not hand-edit the path data. Regenerate it from
 * scripts if the name changes again: this is the third name in a week
 * (Paylance, Doorlane, CrowdBuzz) and the artwork is derived from the
 * letters, so a rename is never just a find-and-replace here.
 */

